sessionEndOK      := parseGeminiHookType(ctx, rawHooks, "SessionEnd", &sessionEnd)
// ... (all 11 parses) ...

if sessionStartOK    { sessionStart = removeEntireHooks(sessionStart) }
if sessionEndOK      { sessionEnd   = removeEntireHooks(sessionEnd) }
// ... (all 11 removes) ...

if sessionStartOK { sessionStart = addGeminiHook(sessionStart, "", "entire-session-start", cmdPrefix+"session-start") }
// SessionEnd has two adds — both gated by sessionEndOK:
if sessionEndOK {
    sessionEnd = addGeminiHook(sessionEnd, "exit",   "entire-session-end-exit",   cmdPrefix+"session-end")
    sessionEnd = addGeminiHook(sessionEnd, "logout", "entire-session-end-logout", cmdPrefix+"session-end")
}
// ... (remaining 9 adds) ...

if sessionStartOK {
    if err := marshalGeminiHookType(rawHooks, "SessionStart", sessionStart); err != nil {
        return 0, err
    }
}
if sessionEndOK {
    if err := marshalGeminiHookType(rawHooks, "SessionEnd", sessionEnd); err != nil {
        return 0, err
    }
}
// ... (all 11 marshals) ...
```

**Call-site pattern for `UninstallHooks`** — same structure, no `addGeminiHook` step:
```go
sessionStartOK := parseGeminiHookType(ctx, rawHooks, "SessionStart", &sessionStart)
// ... (all 11 parses) ...

if sessionStartOK { sessionStart = removeEntireHooks(sessionStart) }
// ... (all 11 removes) ...

if sessionStartOK {
    if err := marshalGeminiHookType(rawHooks, "SessionStart", sessionStart); err != nil {
        return err
    }
}
// ... (all 11 marshals) ...
```

**Behavior when a hook type fails to parse:** The raw bytes stay in `rawHooks` and are written to the output file unchanged. Other hook types that parsed successfully are processed normally. For `InstallHooks`, if `SessionStart` fails to parse, `sessionStart` is nil, `getFirstEntireHookCommand(nil)` returns `""` (≠ expectedCmd), the idempotency check does not early-return — but since `sessionStartOK = false`, the marshal is skipped and the raw bytes are still preserved. All other hook types that parsed successfully receive the normal add/remove treatment.

